---
import BlogArticleShell from '../../../components/BlogArticleShell.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonicalPath = '/blog/identifying-phishing-spreadsheet-scams-reps-2026';
const publishedISO = '2026-05-18';
---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="Spotting the 'Slaughterhouse': 2026 Phishing Spreadsheet Scams | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="Security alert exposing common redirect traps and fake spreadsheet hubs designed to steal Kakobuy login credentials and wallet balances."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="Spotting the 'Slaughterhouse': Identifying phishing spreadsheet sites in 2026"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="18 May 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'spreadsheet phishing scams',
    'fake Kakobuy links',
    'dashenseo scam redirect',
    'protecting agent account',
    'reps security alert 2026',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    As the popularity of Kakobuy grows, so does the sophistication of scammers. In 2026, we are seeing a surge in <strong>"Slaughterhouse" sites</strong>—fake spreadsheets that look identical to community favorites but are designed to hijack your session and drain your wallet.
  </p>

  <h2>The "Dashen" Redirect Trap</h2>
  <p>
    A common tactic involves using Google Sites or low-cost domains (like <code>.cc</code> or <code>.top</code>) that promise "10,000+ Best Finds." When you click a link, instead of going to a marketplace, you are redirected through a series of trackers (e.g., <code>daohang3.dashenseo.cc</code>) that attempt to capture your browser cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>How to spot a fake spreadsheet</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>The "Login Wall":</strong> If a spreadsheet asks you to "Sign in with Kakobuy" to see the links, <strong>CLOSE THE TAB.</strong> Real spreadsheets never need your login.</li>
    <li><strong>URL Mismatch:</strong> Always check the address bar. If you think you are on <code>kakobuy-cn.com</code> but the URL says <code>kakobuy-finds-free.net</code>, it's a scam.</li>
    <li><strong>Forced Redirects:</strong> If clicking a shoe link takes you to a "VPN Download" or "Verify you are human" page first, your data is being harvested.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What to do if you clicked</h2>
  <p>
    If you suspect you've used a compromised link:
    1. Change your Kakobuy password immediately.
    2. Enable <strong>Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)</strong> in your user settings.
    3. Clear your browser cache and cookies.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Stay Safe:</strong> Only use spreadsheets from trusted community hubs. For more on safe sharing, see our <a href="/blog/google-sheets-sharing-spreadsheet-curator-opsec/">Google Sheets opsec guide</a>.
  </p>
</BlogArticleShell>
